{"kind":"assert","text":"Amendment to planner decision a692fd0d, point 5 (sequenced scopes), after review 44ad8b0d F1 to F4 on the corrections head. A refused sequenced delivery is not a positionless entry: it is prepared and committed at its position like an applied judgment. The prepare entry wraps the delivery with decision refused and the reason, holds its reads and rule answers, derives no effects and one send (the result), takes the position, resolves and commits under the existing fence, reservation, resume and replay rules; the commit is the deciding entry, dispatches the result and answers duplicates. A refused sequenced act is as the landed note says (hole at P, nothing in the member). Before allocation, a delivery is answered unavailable with a reason that can change (scope-full, forming) and keeps the sender's duty; with order-left or not-a-member it is decided outside the group's order as an unsequenced delivery is. Points 1 to 4 stand, with one restriction from F4: late and spacing are forms of request handlers (tell, relate) only; an advisory handler has no result, and the validator refuses late-on-advisory and spacing-on-advisory. S1 adds that validator refusal; S3 to S5 implement the prepared refusal. Corrections head draft 2 ab41ab96, review d6c1828b."}